    {
      "v": 3,
      "zh": "他们对我说：「那些被掳归回剩下的人在犹大省遭大难，受凌辱；并且耶路撒冷的城墙拆毁，城门被火焚烧。」",
      "en": "They said to me, “The remnant that remains from the exile there in the province are experiencing considerable[NOTE:1] adversity and reproach. The wall of Jerusalem lies breached, and its gates have been burned down!”[NOTE:2]",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “great.”",
        "Heb “have been burned with fire” (so also in Neh 2:17). The expression “burned with fire” is redundant in contemporary English; the translation uses “burned down” for stylistic reasons."
