    {
      "v": 5,
      "zh": "「耶和华―天上的　神，大而可畏的　神啊，你向爱你、守你诫命的人守约施慈爱。",
      "en": "Then I said, “Please, O Lord God of heaven, great and awesome God, who keeps his loving covenant[NOTE:1] with those who love him and obey[NOTE:2] his commandments,",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “the covenant and loyal love.” The phrase is a hendiadys: the first noun retains its full nominal sense, while the second noun functions adjectivally (“loyal love” = loving). Alternately, the first might function adjectivally and the second noun function as the noun: “covenant and loyal love” = covenant fidelity (see Neh 9:32).",
        "Heb “keep.” The Hebrew verb שָׁמַר (shamar, “to observe; to keep”) is often used as an idiom that means “to obey” the commandments of God (e.g., Exod 20:6; Deut 5:16; 23:24; 29:8; Judg 2:22; 1 Kgs 2:43; 11:11; Ps 119:8, 17, 34; Jer 35:18; Ezek 17:14; Amos 2:4). See BDB 1036 s.v. 3.c."
      ],
